      {
        "number": 3,
        "instructionsHtml": "Section 3<p>Listen and answer questions 21–30.</p>",
        "groups": [
          {
            "id": "part-3-group-1",
            "type": "mcq",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "rubricHtml": "<h3>Questions 21–25</h3><p>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</p><p><strong>Cities built by the sea</strong></p>",
            "questions": [
              {
                "number": 21,
                "textHtml": "Carla and Rob were surprised to learn that coastal cities",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "contain nearly half the world's population."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "include most of the world's largest cities."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "are growing twice as fast as other cities."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 22,
                "textHtml": "According to Rob, building coastal cities near to rivers",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "may bring pollution to the cities."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "may reduce the land available for agriculture."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "may mean the countryside is spoiled by industry."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 23,
                "textHtml": "What mistake was made when building water drainage channels in Miami in the 1950s?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "There were not enough of them."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "They were made of unsuitable materials."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "They did not allow for the effects of climate change."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 24,
                "textHtml": "What do Rob and Carla think that the authorities in Miami should do immediately?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "take measures to restore ecosystems"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "pay for a new flood prevention system"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "stop disposing of waste materials into the ocean"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 25,
                "textHtml": "What do they agree should be the priority for international action?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "greater coordination of activities"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "more sharing of information"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "agreement on shared policies"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
